## Core equations

**Coherence matrix S (Eq. 4-5, unnumbered pre-Eq. 6):**

\\[
S_{ik} = \frac{\partial p'_i}{\partial \phi_k}
\\]

with the coherence measure built from tr(S S^T).

**Interference measure — general (Eq. 6):**

\\[
I(P) \;=\; \sum_{i,k,l} |P_{ii,kl}|^2 \;-\; \sum_{i,k} |P_{ii,kk}|^2
\\]

**Operator-sum reformulation (Eq. 7):**

\\[
I \;=\; \sum_{i,k,m} \left| \sum_l (E_l)_{ik} (E_l^*)_{im} \right|^2 \;-\; \sum_{i,k} \left( \sum_l |(E_l)_{ik}|^2 \right)^2
\\]

**Unitary case (Eq. 8) — with P_{ii,kl} = U_{ik} U_{il}^*:**

\\[
I(P(U)) \;=\; N \;-\; \sum_{i,k=1}^{N} |U_{ik}|^4
\\]

with bounds \\(0 \le I(P(U)) \le N-1\\).

**i-bit definition (Sec. IV.A.4):**

\\[
n_I \;=\; \log_2(I(P(U)) + 1)
\\]

so that a single Hadamard (I = 1) → n_I = 1, and \\(W_n = H^{\otimes n}\\) with
I = 2^n - 1 → n_I = n i-bits.

**Beam splitter (Sec. IV.C):**

\\[
I(P(U_{BS}(\theta))) \;=\; 2\left(1 - \cos^4\theta - \sin^4\theta\right)
\\]

**Bit-flip after Hadamard (Sec. IV.D):**

\\[
I \;=\; (1 - 2p)^2
\\]

**Grover asymptotic "actually used" (Sec. IV.F, following Eq. after Fig. 7):**

\\[
I_{\text{used}} \;=\; 8 - \tfrac{24}{N} + O(N^{-2})
\\]

## Key numeric values reported in the paper

- Identity, X, Y, Z, CNOT, SWAP, CCX, and any classical permutation of the
  computational basis: I = 0.
- Hadamard (1 qubit): I = 1 (one i-bit).
- Walsh-Hadamard W_n: I = 2^n − 1 (n i-bits).
- QFT_n on N = 2^n basis states: I = N − 1 (saturates the upper bound).
- Beam splitter at θ = π/4: I = 1 (equivalent to Hadamard up to phases).
- Teleportation encoder: I = 6 (paper reports "about 2.58 i-bits", from
  log₂(6) = 2.585 — a minor convention slip; rigorous n_I = log₂(7) = 2.807).
- Grover for n = 8 qubits: I(full unitary) ≈ 2^n − 2 = 254 (Fig. 6);
  "actually used" (with W_n stripped) tends to ≈ 8 (~3 i-bits asymptotically).
- Shor for R = 15 (Fig. 4): accumulated I grows exponentially in the last
  (QFT) part and reaches 2n − 2L (n qubits, L = ⌈log₂ R⌉).
